## Blog social previews

Hugo generates a 1200×630 PNG for each post using its title and date. The
`social-image.html` partial uses the bundled fonts and `assets/social/background.png`;
there are no network requests or extra image-generation dependencies. The image
URL changes with its content. Other pages retain the site's default image.
Posts use their description or an excerpt for social preview text.

After building, check the image files and metadata with:

```sh
node scripts/check-social-images.mjs public
```

Post canonical URLs use Hugo's published permalink, including the trailing slash.
Netlify redirects the URL without a trailing slash to that address. Run URL
checkers against the final URL after redirects; comparing a redirect's input
URL to the destination's canonical will report an intentional difference.
The verification script also checks canonical URLs and the PNG favicon. To
validate a build with a different base URL, pass it as a second argument.

